run "type gate (mypy)" python3 -m substrate.type_gate --quiet

# ⟡stub-authority — every `.pyi` in stubs/ must still match the module it describes.  A stub
# lets a promoted module import an authority that is not yet a package (mypy_path finds the
# `.pyi`), which buys real safety and opens a real hole: nothing otherwise notices when the
# module moves and the stub does not.  NOT a ratchet — a BIJECTION: a stub either matches or it
